    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d44">

                <pb facs="0150" n="134" sameAs="frus:frus1949v06/pg134"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">890F.6363/6–1049: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Chargé in the United Kingdom</hi> (<hi
                        rendition="#italic">Holmes</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of
                        State </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">confidential</hi>
                    </seg>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">London</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1949-06-10T19:00:00+01:00">June 10, 1949—7 p.
                            m.</date>
                    </dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>2249. Embassy’s 2130, June 1.<anchor n="1" xml:id="d44-f1"/> Re offshore oil
                    Chadwiek said today Sheikhs of Bahrein, Kuwait and Qatar issued their
                    proclamations <pb facs="0151" n="135" xml:id="pg135"/> on or about June 4 and
                    that remainder would be out soon in standard form. British Ambassadors Tehran
                    and Baghdad have informed two Govts re proclamations. Iraqis inquired who had
                    put Saudi Arabian Govt up to issuing proclamation and were told by British
                    Ambassador that he understood it drafted with assistance ARAMCO.</p>
                <p>2. Chadwick said he knew of no letters of intent for offshore oil having been
                    granted by Sheikhs.<anchor n="2" xml:id="d44-f2"/>
                </p>
                <p>Sent Dept 2249, repeated Baghdad 48, Jidda 43, Tehran 69, Dhahran 8.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Holmes</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d44-f1" n="1" xml:id="d44-f1-content">
                <p>Not printed.</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d44-f2" n="2" xml:id="d44-f2-content">
                <p>Dhahran, on July 23 and August 8, transmitted to the Department the Arabic texts
                    and the English translations of the seabed proclamations issued by Bahrein,
                    Qatar, and the Trucial Sheikhdoms on or about June 5. (despatches 106 and 116,
                    890.0145/7–2349,/8–849) The earlier despatch noted that the proclamations were
                    issued in Arabic but were “translations from the original English prepared In
                    uniform language by the British Government. The Political Resident in Bahrein
                    had translations made into Arabic at the Residency in Bahrein.” Dhahran, on
                    August 10, transmitted the original text in English used by the Political
                    Residency as a model in preparing the proclamations (despatch 117,
                    890.0145/8–1049).</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
